ew hope. ... Publisher  | Eden Project Books, 2006\n\n### About the author (2006)\n\nJames Martin studied physics at Oxford, served in the British Army and then joined IBM in Paris as a systems engineer. He lectures and writes extensively on management and technology. He is the author of the Pulitzer-nominated The Wired Society (1977), famous for the author’s remarkably accurate predictions about technology and the Internet. In Technology’s Crucible (1987), he alludes to Arab terrorists and a major attack on New York in 1998.\n\n### Bibliographic information\n\nTitle  | The Meaning of the 21st Century: A Vital Blueprint for Ensuring Our Future\nAuthor  | James Martin\nEdition  | illustrated\nPublisher  | Eden Project Books, 2006\nISBN  | 1903919851, 9781903919859\nLength  | 431 pages\nSubjects  | History › Modern › 21st Century\nBusiness & Economics / Exports & Imports\nHistory / Modern / 21st Century\nNature / Environmental Conservation & Protection\nSocial Science / Future Studies\nTechnology & Engineering / General--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nThe Meaning of the 21st Century: A Vital Blueprint for Ensuring Our Future - James Martin - Google Books (https://books.google.com/books/about/The_Meaning_of_the_21st_Century.html?id=79DmisPF3dMC)\nciteturn111search1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 1.2 years ago; # The Meaning of the 21st Century: A Vital Blueprint for Ensuring Our FutureImage: Front Cover James Martin Eden Project Books, 2006 - Business & Economics - 431 pages Argues that we are living at a turning point in human history and that it is in the scientific breakthroughs of the new century that we will find new hope. ... Publisher  | Eden Project Books, 2006\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nThe meaning of the 21st century by James Martin | Open Library (https://openlibrary.org/books/OL3432166M/The_meaning_of_the_21st_century)\nciteturn111search2 [wordlim: 200] P